<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
      Elijah has just stood on Mount Carmel.<break time="500ms"/>
      He has called down fire from heaven in front of all the people.<break time="500ms"/>
      The false prophets of Baal have been defeated.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The rain has returned to the land after years of drought.<break time="1800ms"/>

      It was the greatest day of his life.<break time="500ms"/>
      He stood alone before the crowd and God answered with fire.<break time="1000ms"/>
      No one could deny what had happened.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But now a message arrives.<break time="500ms"/>
      Queen Jezebel sends word.<break time="500ms"/>
      By this time tomorrow, she says, your life will be like the lives of those prophets.<break time="1000ms"/>
      She means to kill him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And Elijah, the man who faced down hundreds without flinching, is afraid.<break time="500ms"/>
      Deeply afraid.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Not the sharp fear of a moment, but the heavy fear that comes after you have given everything you have.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He runs.<break time="500ms"/>
      He leaves his servant behind.<break time="500ms"/>
      He goes a day's journey into the wilderness, alone.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The man who stood tall on the mountain now stumbles into the desert with nothing left.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes the bravest people are the ones who break the hardest.<break time="500ms"/>
      Sometimes the strongest season is followed by the emptiest.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Elijah has nothing left to give.<break time="1800ms"/>
      And he runs.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
